        "edge_cases": "The \u03bc=0 branch uses the stated massless-apex convention; \u03bc>0 uses the SI rest-mass conversion. Only Schwartz-smearing is defined, and no point-field operator is introduced.",
        "well_definedness": "The unit and field dimensions are fixed by def-qft-framework-units; the matrix and projection formulas by def-qft-dirac-projections and lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices; the Fock/CAR and field map by def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces, lem-qft-fock-ccr-car and lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality. The postulate supplies only the physical assignment. The latter math suppliers are draft with current escalated readiness, so this carrier remains conditional."
      },
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "post-qft-free-field-model",
          "source_section": "Postulate",
          "quote": "As the physical interpretation of this selected free model, assign the real scalar species to the bosonic symmetric Fock representation and assign the Dirac field to the particle/antiparticle CAR representation on $\\mathcal H_+\\oplus\\overline{\\mathcal H_-}$. Choose the zero-particle Fock vectors as the scalar and Dirac vacuum states.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-qft-framework-units",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For a species with rest mass $m_{\\rm rest,SI}>0$ in kilograms define its inverse-length mass parameter $$\\mu:=\\frac{m_{\\rm rest,SI}c}{\\hbar}\\quad[\\mathrm m^{-1}].$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-qft-dirac-projections",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "$h_D(\\mathbf k)=\\sum_j\\alpha_j k_j+\\beta\\mu$",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-qft-dirac-projection-matrices",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every $\\mu\\ge0$ and almost every $\\mathbf k$, the displayed Pauli blocks satisfy $h_D(\\mathbf k)^\\dagger=h_D(\\mathbf k)$, $h_D(\\mathbf k)^2=\\omega(\\mathbf k)^2I_4$, and $P_\\pm(\\mathbf k)$ are complementary orthogonal projections of rank two.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The bosonic and fermionic Fock Hilbert spaces are the square-summable direct sums",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The fermionic $c(h)$ and $c^\\dagger(h)$ extend to bounded operators on the whole Fock space, with norms $\\|h\\|$, and satisfy on the whole space",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then $u_F\\in\\mathcal H_D$, continuously in the Schwartz topology, and $$\\Psi(F)=c(P_+u_F)+c^\\dagger(\\overline{P_-u_F})$$ defines a bounded operator on $\\mathcal F_a(\\mathcal H_+\\oplus\\overline{\\mathcal H_-})$, antilinear in $F$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A2",
          "source": "def-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following statement.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "d-1.1",
