      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-57",
        "notes": "Independently read Definition and Verification 1.1\u20132.1 and all eight direct suppliers. Pauli-block h_D squares to omega squared; complementary bounded projections have closed separable ranges, including the null massless-apex convention. CAR operators are bounded on antisymmetric Fock space under Countable Choice. The Schwartz decay estimate in the CAR-locality supplier makes u_F continuous in L2; annihilation is antilinear and conjugate-space creation is antilinear, with norm at most sqrt(2)||u_F||. Length coordinate t in this Fourier formula is the increment defined by def-qft-dirac-projections, and SI energy is hbar c omega. Species, vacuum and CAR assignment are adopted; no point-field or empirical/general spin-statistics inference. Reader/refuter have no findings. Existing upstream readiness holds remain open; this review does not certify those suppliers."
