          "id": "d-2.1",
          "claim": "Conjugation is multiplicative, so a product of r field generators gains the factor (-1)^r; every even-degree monomial is fixed. Products and adjoints of even monomials remain even, so finite linear combinations with the identity form a unital *-algebra, and linearity fixes the whole algebraic span.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d-3.1",
          "claim": "Unitary conjugation preserves operator norm, so the invariance extends to norm limits of bounded even polynomials; the 4\u03c0 identity is immediate from the supplied Fock action.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
