          "reason": "Example of Two-pi spin rotation and even-observable invariance: Define $\\mathcal A_D^{\\mathrm{even}}$ as the norm closure of finite linear combinations of the identity and even-degree products of $\\Psi(F)$ and $\\Psi(F)^\\dagger$, for Schwartz spinor tests $F$. In the selected free Dirac model, let $U_{2\\pi}$ implement a spatial rotation by $2\\pi$ and let $U_{4\\pi}$ implement a rotation by $4\\pi$. Then $U_{2\\pi}=(-1)^N$: it is $-I$ on odd-particle sectors and $+I$ on even-particle sectors, while $U_{4\\pi}=I$. Every finite even polynomial in bounded spacetime-smeared Dirac fields and their adjoints is invariant under conjugation by $U_{2\\pi}$, and therefore so is $\\mathcal A_D^{\\mathrm{even}}$. This is an exact model calculation; it does not infer a general spin-statistics the The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
